import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 434 | Dragon Ball · Historical Regression Necessity: Strong One Absent and Civilization Collapses","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 434 | Dragon Ball · Historical Regression Necessity: Strong One Absent and Civilization Collapses","no":434,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Historical Regression","Civilization Collapse","Goku","Institutional Absence"],"related":["03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","20-Anchor Structure and Hierarchy","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0434_模块2-龙珠-历史倒退必然性-强者缺位文明即崩溃.md","filePath":"en/0434_模块2-龙珠-历史倒退必然性-强者缺位文明即崩溃.md"}'),a={name:"en/0434_模块2-龙珠-历史倒退必然性-强者缺位文明即崩溃.md"};function s(r,e,l,c,u,d){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-434-dragon-ball-·-historical-regression-necessity-strong-one-absent-and-civilization-collapses" tabindex="-1">Entry 434 | Dragon Ball · Historical Regression Necessity: Strong One Absent and Civilization Collapses <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-434-dragon-ball-·-historical-regression-necessity-strong-one-absent-and-civilization-collapses" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 434 | Dragon Ball · Historical Regression Necessity: Strong One Absent and Civilization Collapses&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 3) | Benchmark base: Documents 03, 20, 49</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-after-every-great-war-civilization-starts-from-zero" tabindex="-1">Introduction: after every great war, civilization starts from zero <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-after-every-great-war-civilization-starts-from-zero" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: after every great war, civilization starts from zero&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s historical view: whether a civilization is mature is not by how strong its strongest is, but by whether it can still run when the strongest is absent. Dragon Ball world is precisely this standard&#39;s negative specimen — its civilization curve is not ascending, but &quot;destroy—wish-rebuild—destroy again—wish-rebuild again&quot; cycle. This entry, by the law-first axiom (law precedes, never retcons) and collective ascension axiom (strong ones feed back to Myriad Ranks; no great-material-wasted), dissects why Dragon Ball world is &quot;strong one present and civilization present; strong one gone and civilization collapses.&quot;</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball world&#39;s energy waste, the most glaring manifestation, is <strong>strong ones never legislate for civilization</strong>:</p><ul><li>Goku defeats King Piccolo, yet established no &quot;anti-demon-invasion early-warning mechanism&quot;</li><li>Goku defeats Frieza, yet pushed no &quot;anti-Frieza-army international convention&quot;</li><li>Goku defeats Cell, Buu, yet left no &quot;what if Majin revives next time&quot; contingency plan</li><li>Even Piccolo, Kami, Supreme Kai these &quot;gods,&quot; never formulated a cosmos-tier civilization governance framework</li></ul><p>Energy all sedimented in muscle memory; institutional construction zero.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball world&#39;s historical regression is structurally inevitable:</p><ol><li><strong>Revival erases history</strong>: Dragon Ball wishes revive the dead, restore cities; civilization has no true &quot;trauma memory&quot;; next time the same mistake is repeated — this is the causal self-discipline axiom&#39;s complete opposite</li><li><strong>Commoners no armed ability</strong>: Earth ordinary people in the Saiyan arc could only hide in houses; by Cell, Buu arcs directly one-shot killed; civilization has no self-organized defense</li><li><strong>God-tier stratum does not legislate</strong>: Supreme Kai only &quot;observes,&quot; God of Destruction only &quot;destroys,&quot; Zeno only &quot;wipes the table&quot; — the whole cosmos has no &quot;governor&quot; role</li><li><strong>Technology single-point dependency</strong>: Capsule Corp, Bulma&#39;s family is Earth&#39;s only tech engine; Bulma stays home, Earth tech does not advance</li><li><strong>School and education broken</strong>: Gohan was a scholar seedling, yet repeatedly pulled back to the battlefield by wars; Earth has no public system to cultivate next-generation cultivators</li></ol><p>Conclusion: <strong>Dragon Ball world&#39;s &quot;peace&quot; was never institutional product, but villains not attacking yet.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking on the &quot;historical regression&quot; dimension manifests as <strong>irresponsibility for civilization&#39;s future</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Father absent</strong>: Gohan, Goten&#39;s growth repeatedly interrupted by Goku&#39;s &quot;want to fight again&quot;; after Goku died he should cultivate in Other World, yet repeatedly runs back to the human world &quot;to see old friends&quot;</li><li><strong>No successor cultivation</strong>: Goku only circles in the &quot;can beat then beat, can&#39;t then train more&quot; loop; never systematically cultivated a next generation that could take over Earth after he dies</li><li><strong>Treats cosmos as playground</strong>: Tournament of Power, Zeno&#39;s arena; Goku&#39;s every &quot;I want to trade blows with the strong&quot; bets the whole cosmos&#39;s survival — this is treating Myriad Ranks&#39; fate as personal hobby</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Civilization Vacuum</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Goku wins and it scatters</td><td>Anchor Council legislates; after war must pass &quot;disaster review and defense act&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Dragon Ball wish revival</td><td>Causal self-discipline axiom: revival must be filed; trauma memory retained; history must not be erased</td></tr><tr><td>Commoners no armed ability</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republican co-build; basic methods universal; commoners have self-organization ability</td></tr><tr><td>God-tier stratum does not legislate</td><td>Symbiotic Executive Committee + Symbiotic Court; separation of powers; governance enshrined</td></tr><tr><td>Goku alone carries</td><td>20% activation strategy; strong ones emerge in batches, not one person dominating</td></tr><tr><td>Schools broken</td><td>Symbiotic education system (Doc 037); cultivation knowledge textbook-ified, public-ified</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball civilization curve — every 5 years a &quot;destroyed by villain—wish-rebuild&quot; cycle</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;Goku dies in battle not returning,&quot; &quot;Goku establishes Earth Defense Force,&quot; &quot;Goku in Other World not coming back&quot; three controls</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Earth civilization&#39;s survival years under Goku absence, commoner casualty rate, Namek reconstruction rate</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Civilization Single-Point Dependence Collapse Timeline</em>, quantifying &quot;if Goku truly died in the Cell arc, how many more years could Earth hold&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: low</strong>. &quot;Dragon Balls can revive people&quot; early had limits (one-year lifespan, only one wish); late limits repeatedly broken: Namekian Dragon Balls can grant three wishes, Frieza revived, Cell revived, Buu&#39;s pure good revived… revival rules entirely serve plot</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extremely high</strong>. GT turns Goku back into a child, Super rewrites Earth timeline back to &quot;Goku still a martial artist,&quot; Heroes directly cross-temporal — historical regression in Dragon Ball series is not civilizational disease, but writers&#39; common tool</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Civilization survival entirely bet on Goku; no institutional backup</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: god-tier strong ones never legislate for civilization; energy zero institutional spillover</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: revival wishes erase civilization&#39;s trauma memory; this is predation of history itself</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least left Peerless Academy&#39;s institutional legacy; Goku left nothing</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Earth commoners, Namekians, Galaxy Force in disasters all protected objects, not co-build subjects</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Dragon Ball world&#39;s &quot;cosmos&quot; always locked by God-of-Destruction—Zeno pyramid; no jurisprudential channel to expand outward</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball world&#39;s historical regression is not accident, but design. Every &quot;peace&quot; is built on the gamble that &quot;Goku can transform next time&quot;; every &quot;rebuild&quot; relies on wiping history and starting over. What Heng Yuan Zhou wants to ask: what if Dragon Balls can no longer grant wishes? What if Goku did not make it back this time? Dragon Ball series in forty years never answered these two questions — because its worldview never intended to let civilization stand on its own. Making civilization not depend on any one Goku is the true exit.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · historical regression necessity · strong one absent and civilization collapses described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./432_模块2-龙珠-总论悟空与战力膨胀体系定性.html">Entry 432 · Overview</a> · <a href="./464_模块2-龙珠-平民处境-普通人在战力世界的无助.html">Entry 464 · Commoners&#39; Situation</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const m=i(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
